   * Records an outcome and does not give up. A handler has already run, so its
   * outcome is worth more than anything else this worker could be doing: when the
   * queue is busy or the disk fails, wait and try again until it is recorded or
   * the job turns out to belong to someone else. Repeating is safe, because a
   * call that did reach the log answers the second time with the same outcome.
